# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD diff-1 6573 darkgray
WHY Starts the build with the 24/16-tooth differential housing that the whole mechanism sits in.

STEP 2
ADD bevel-1 6589 tan
ADD bevel-2 6589 tan
ADD bevel-3 6589 tan
CONNECT bevel-1.axlehole1 -> diff-1.bar1? LOCKED
CONNECT bevel-2.axlehole1 -> diff-1.bar1? LOCKED
CONNECT bevel-3.axlehole1 -> diff-1.bar1? LOCKED
WHY Slots the three small bevel gears onto the housing's internal cross bar so they can spin as the differential's pinions.

STEP 3
ADD frame-1 64179 lightgray
ADD axle-1 4519 lightgray
ADD axle-2 4519 lightgray
CONNECT axle-1.axle1 -> diff-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT axle-2.axle1 -> diff-1.hole2 TURNS
WHY Fits a short axle stub into each side of the housing, then wraps the open H-shaped frame around the whole assembly.

STEP 4
ADD axle-3 4519 lightgray
CONNECT axle-3.axle1 -> frame-1.hole10~ TURNS
WHY Adds a bearing axle through the frame's side hole, ready to carry the output gear.

STEP 5
ADD bevel-4 6589 tan
CONNECT bevel-4.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Locks the fourth bevel gear onto the bearing axle so it meshes with the housing's outer teeth as the differential's output.

STEP 6
ADD connector-1 6553 lightgray
CONNECT connector-1.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle3 LOCKED
WHY Caps the output axle with the perpendicular-axle connector, finishing the differential as a compact output stub.
